Levels marking
Level 1 (1–3 marks) Statements including limited detail which describe the
consequences of overpopulation for a country.
Level 2 (4–6 marks)
Uses named example.
More developed statements which describe the consequences of
overpopulation for a country.
(Note: Max 5 if no named or inappropriate example)
Level 3 (7 marks)
Uses named example.
Comprehensive and accurate statements which describe the consequences
of overpopulation for a country, including some place-specific reference.
Content Guide
Problems such as:
Exhaustion of natural resources;
Pressure on/increased demand for food;
Pressure on/increased demand for water supplies/lack of fresh water
supplies;
Pressure on fuel/power supplies;
Traffic congestion;
Lack of housing/temporary accommodation/overcrowded
housing/homelessness/refugee camps/squatter settlements/shanty towns;
