Levels marking
Level 1 (1–3 marks)
Statements including limited detail which describe the features of a delta
and/or explain how it is formed.
Level 2 (4–6 marks)
More developed or linked statements which describe the features of a delta
and/or explain how it is formed.
Level 3 (7 marks)
Comprehensive and accurate statements using appropriate terminology,
which describe the features of a delta and explain how it is formed.
Content Guide
Description is likely to include reference to:
Shape;
Flat land;
Distributaries;
Slow speed of flow;
etc.
Explanation:
River carries large load;
Speed of flow reduced;
Deposition;
River splits/goes around deposits/distributaries;
Flocculation;
Currents unable to remove sediment/sediment builds up;
Colonisation by vegetation;
etc.
Only credit ideas on diagram if labelled.
